{
  "summary": "Clamps transaction entry timestamps loaded from mempool.dat to the current time if they are in the future. This prevents loaded transactions from bypassing expiration under -mempoolexpiry when a node's clock moves backward across a restart.",
  "problem": "When loading transactions from mempool.dat, entries recorded with timestamps ahead of the current system clock are accepted as-is. Those transactions will not expire within the duration configured by -mempoolexpiry, remaining in the mempool longer than expected or indefinitely.",
  "evidence": [
    "Author provides a functional test in test/functional/mempool_persist.py demonstrating that without clamping, a transaction written with a future timestamp preserves that future time across a restart with a stepped-back clock (PR description and commit c07124e5b5)."
  ],
