  "changed_since_previous": "Diff and commit hash are now available; the implementation adds a std::min clamp in LoadMempool and a dedicated functional test in mempool_persist.py.",
  "card": "Clamps future timestamps to the current time when loading mempool entries from mempool.dat. Transactions loaded with timestamps in the future currently evade time-based expiry under -mempoolexpiry until the clock catches up. The author demonstrates the issue with a functional test where a node restarts with its clock set earlier than the saved entry time. Open PR #36540 proposes removing time-based mempool expiry entirely, which would make this change moot.",
